input.newString:
// Delivers webhook events to billing-provider.
//
// DO NOT ADD RETRIES TO THIS PATH.
//
// Retrying `/webhooks/billing` is unsafe. That endpoint has no idempotency
// key, so a retry can be processed as a second, separate charge rather than
// a redelivery of the same event.
//
// We learned this the hard way. An exponential-backoff retry loop was added
// here (commit 207d272) to smooth over intermittent 502s, then reverted
// (commit 39db4f3): during the 2023-11-14 outage it amplified load and
// double-charged 1,842 customers, all of whom had to be refunded manually.
//
// Reliability must come from the durable delivery queue, which can
// deduplicate by event id before handing an event to this dispatcher.
// Only revisit retries here once billing-provider supports an idempotency
// key *and* this call sends one on every attempt.
async function deliver(io, event) {
  const res = await io.post('/webhooks/billing', event);
  return res;
}

